{"aligned_passages":[{"anchor":"hypothesis-specific-obstructions","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:0f219e7bffa9a7fd19ae5e29b6712a52433038999248a52795a946ab77beb187/papers/long.json","paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=a95759ce5c96e8226b9411d42d1138f4b439d3c1a2e4ebf7160579b702e450e1","passage_ref":"sha256:9db121aa3907c3f1a8a48d6797094bb13e0c3efb5c7f42f8664bb4e6fba1025c/papers/long.md/sha256:0f219e7bffa9a7fd19ae5e29b6712a52433038999248a52795a946ab77beb187/papers/long.json/passages/hypothesis-specific-obstructions","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=a95759ce5c96e8226b9411d42d1138f4b439d3c1a2e4ebf7160579b702e450e1&paper=long&passage=hypothesis-specific-obstructions","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=a95759ce5c96e8226b9411d42d1138f4b439d3c1a2e4ebf7160579b702e450e1&paper=long&passage=hypothesis-specific-obstructions","span":{"end_byte":420549,"end_line":3870,"start_byte":391783,"start_line":3634},"stage":"long"}],"lenses":{"consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=a95759ce5c96e8226b9411d42d1138f4b439d3c1a2e4ebf7160579b702e450e1&view=arguments&node=long.thm-cd-neg3-impossible&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=a95759ce5c96e8226b9411d42d1138f4b439d3c1a2e4ebf7160579b702e450e1&node=long.thm-cd-neg3-impossible&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=a95759ce5c96e8226b9411d42d1138f4b439d3c1a2e4ebf7160579b702e450e1&node=long.thm-cd-neg3-impossible&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=a95759ce5c96e8226b9411d42d1138f4b439d3c1a2e4ebf7160579b702e450e1&view=arguments&node=long.thm-cd-neg3-impossible&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=a95759ce5c96e8226b9411d42d1138f4b439d3c1a2e4ebf7160579b702e450e1&ref=sha256%3A5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1%2Fnodes%2Flong.thm-cd-neg3-impossible","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"The evidence mapping records a Lean proof of exactly this statement. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-cd-neg3-impossible"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-cd-neg3-impossible"],"id":"long.thm-cd-neg3-impossible","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 10.6 ($`C_D=-3`$ is impossible at the final middle transition, $`D\\ge 13`$)","locator":"Long record Theorem 10.6, p. 115, label thm:cd-neg3-impossible","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Consider a hypothetical *final middle transition*: a middle transition at row $D\\ge 13$ ($\\lnot\\mathrm{carries}$, and the middle-branch inequality $4\\mathrm{rem}(D)+\\mathrm{gap}-\\mathrm{belowPulse} < \\mathrm{terminalWeight}$ holds at $D$), followed by an all-right tail forever after ($\\forall s\\ge D{+}1$, $\\mathrm{seamGreedyWord}(s+1) =\n\\mathrm{seamGreedyWord}(s).\\mathrm{extend}\\ \\mathrm{true}$). Under these assumptions,\n$$\n\\mathrm{belowPulse}(D) + 2 \\;\\le\\; 4\\cdot\\mathrm{rem}(D),\n$$\ni.e. $C_D \\ge -2$ ; the cell $C_D=-3$ (and every more negative value) is excluded.*\n\n***Proof of the bound.** The all-right-tail assumption puts the terminal-augmented finite prefix strictly above $1/2$. Consequently the producer carry is below its complete incidence tail, or equivalently $Z_D<1+1/(2^D-1)$, where $Z_D=\\mathrm{rem}(D)-\\mathrm{seamWordFloorError}(D)$. The lower bound uses the other endpoint: under the same tail assumption, the finite value at $D$ plus the complete Mersenne tail remains below $1/2$. The exact scaled remainder identity therefore gives\n$$\nZ_D>4^D\\sum_{e>D}\\frac1{2^e-1}-2^D>\\frac13.\n$$\nThe last inequality follows by retaining the first two geometric channels of the complete Mersenne tail. Put $E_D=\\mathrm{seamWordFloorError}(D)$. Pulse absorption gives $\\mathrm{belowPulse}(D)\\le4E_D$, so\n$$\n4\\,\\mathrm{rem}(D)-\\mathrm{belowPulse}(D)\n \\ge4(\\mathrm{rem}(D)-E_D)=4Z_D>\\frac43.\n$$\nThe left side is an integer, hence is at least $2$, as required. The upper threshold inequality alone would not give this lower bound.*\n\n***Scope.** This excludes $C_D=-3$ at a middle row $D\\ge13$ under the additional all-right-tail assumption. The general induction requires exclusion of all three cells at every middle row, not just under this extra hypothesis, together with its right-branch bound. The two statements share the same coordinate $C_D$ but have different hypotheses. Theorem 10.6 is universal over rows satisfying the additional all-right-tail assumption; it does not assert that such a row exists. The induction hypothesis concerns every middle row, without that tail assumption. Excluding $C_D=-3$ in the former statement therefore does not supply the exclusion required in the latter. **Object or representation:** about the *object* under the stated hypothesis ; a genuine arithmetic consequence of the all-right-tail assumption via the fatal-gap orbit, not a coordinate artifact.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.thm-cd-neg3-impossible","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.thm-cd-neg3-impossible","id":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.thm-cd-neg3-impossible%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_final_middle_cell_at_least_neg_two%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.thm-cd-neg3-impossible%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_final_middle_cell_at_least_neg_two%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_final_middle_cell_at_least_neg_two"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":